{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-9","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-9","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.md","line":101,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.tex#def:dc-ch1-2-9","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-8]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.tex","label":"def:dc-ch1-2-9","line":222,"source":"\\begin{definition}[vector field along a curve; length]\n  \\label{def:dc-ch1-2-9}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch1-2-1, def:dc-ch1-2-8}\n\n  \\dcref{ch1:2.9}\n  A \\emph{vector field along a curve} $c:I\\to M$ is a differentiable assignment\n  $V(t)\\in T_{c(t)}M$, where differentiability means that $t\\mapsto V(t)f$ is\n  differentiable for every differentiable $f$ on $M$. The velocity field is\n  $dc(\\frac{d}{dt})=\\frac{dc}{dt}$. For $[a,b]\\subset I$, the restriction is a\n  \\emph{segment} and its length is\n  $$\n  \\ell_a^b(c)=\\int_a^b\\left\\langle\\frac{dc}{dt},\\frac{dc}{dt}\\right\\rangle^{1/2}\\,dt.\n  $$\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[vector field along a curve; length] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a64632d6368312d322d39\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_RiemannianMetrics%23def%3Adc-ch1-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch1-2-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_RiemannianMetrics%23def%3Adc-ch1-2-8\">↗ def:dc-ch1-2-8</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch1:2.9</span></span>A <em>vector field along a curve</em> <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c:I\\to M$\">$c:I\\to M$</span> is a differentiable assignment <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V(t)\\in T_{c(t)}M$\">$V(t)\\in T_{c(t)}M$</span>, where differentiability means that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\mapsto V(t)f$\">$t\\mapsto V(t)f$</span> is differentiable for every differentiable <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>. The velocity field is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dc(\\frac{d}{dt})=\\frac{dc}{dt}$\">$dc(\\frac{d}{dt})=\\frac{dc}{dt}$</span>. For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[a,b]\\subset I$\">$[a,b]\\subset I$</span>, the restriction is a <em>segment</em> and its length is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\ell _a^b(c)=\\int _a^b\\left\\langle \\frac{dc}{dt},\\frac{dc}{dt}\\right\\rangle ^{1/2}\\, dt.  \\]\">\\[  \\ell _a^b(c)=\\int _a^b\\left\\langle \\frac{dc}{dt},\\frac{dc}{dt}\\right\\rangle ^{1/2}\\, dt.  \\]</span> ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-8","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#lem:dc-ch1-2-9-isom","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch1-2-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-8","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-8","label":"def:dc-ch1-2-8"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#lem:dc-ch1-2-9-isom","title":"lem:dc-ch1-2-9-isom","label":"lem:dc-ch1-2-9-isom"},{"kind":"use